      <span style="font-size: 0.85rem; color: #64748b;">Quick balances:</span>
      <button type="button" class="btn-balance-preset" data-miles="10000">10,000</button>
      <button type="button" class="btn-balance-preset" data-miles="25000">25,000</button>
      <button type="button" class="btn-balance-preset" data-miles="50000">50,000</button>
      <button type="button" class="btn-balance-preset" data-miles="60000">60,000</button>
      <button type="button" class="btn-balance-preset" data-miles="100000">100,000</button>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="field">
    <label for="presetValuation">
      <span>Valuation Scenario (CPM / CPP)<button type="button" class="btn-help-toggle" id="btnHelpScenario" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="helpScenarioGuide">How do I choose?</button></span>
      <span class="hint" id="hintValuation">¢ / Mile</span>
    </label>

    <div id="helpScenarioGuide" class="help-scenario-guide" style="display: none;">
      <h4>How to choose a cents-per-mile assumption:</h4>
      <div class="guide-step">
        <strong>1. Evaluating an immediate redemption:</strong>
        <p>Use your exact flight prices: <code>Realized CPP = [(Cash Ticket Price - Award Taxes) ÷ Miles Required] × 100</code>. Test your specific itinerary in our <a href="/en/calculators/cents-per-point/">CPP Calculator</a>.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="guide-step">
        <strong>2. Modeling domestic economy flights:</strong>
        <p>A conservative benchmark of 1.0¢ to 1.2¢ reflects typical domestic routes subject to peak dynamic award pricing.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="guide-step">
        <strong>3. Modeling international Polaris Business Class or partner sweet spots:</strong>
        <p>Higher-tier redemptions frequently achieve 1.5¢ to 2.0¢+ per mile when Saver award seats are open.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <select id="presetValuation" aria-describedby="hintValuation unitValuation">
      <option value="custom">Custom cents-per-mile assumption</option>
      <option value="1.0">Conservative scenario: 1.0¢ per mile (Domestic short-haul baseline)</option>
      <option value="1.2" selected>Typical airline scenario: 1.2¢ per mile (Standard economy award)</option>
      <option value="1.5">Higher-value scenario: 1.5¢ per mile (Partner award or premium cabin)</option>
    </select>
    <input type="number" id="cppValue" value="1.2" min="0.01" step="0.01" style="margin-top:10px;" inputmode="decimal" aria-describedby="hintValuation unitValuation">
    <div class="unit" id="unitValuation">These CPM values represent educational modeling benchmarks, not official buyback rates or cash guarantee quotes from United Airlines.</div>
  </div>
</div>

